speechtext:
Order. It has been moved by the hon. member for Winnipeg North Centre, seconded by the hon. member for Nanaimo-Cowichan-The Islands;
That this House welcomes the announcement that the Prime Minister will discuss with President Carter, during his forthcoming visit to Washington, the Garrison diversion project in North Dakota, and further that this House unanimously endorses the stand the Prime Minister has said he will take to the effect that work on the Lone Tree reservoir be deferred, pending a review of the whole project and of this country's concern over its effects on Canadian waters, particularly in Manitoba and Saskatchewan, which is being made by the International Joint Commission.
Is it the pleasure of the House to adopt the said motion?
